From 67add62f2c4973ecd413623d52487e1dc7551d6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:09:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Read only the annotation parts whose inputs moved;
 cache board stamps

t_28eb8d66d577eab3. On the hub (serving process, current core) the
kanban-annotation thread ran at 51% CPU and 17,021 voluntary cs/s, and
/api/profiles/sessions had p95 1.7-2.1 s.

Annotation holder. _event_refresh set force_read for the whole scope on
every wake, so each wake recomputed the counts, reprojected the remote
links and re-ran every done check on every recent done card. The hub's
watched files are written about 5 times a second (measured: board WALs
0.3-0.4/s each over 7 boards, kanban.db 1/s, the sync shadow 0.75/s,
state.db 0.35/s), mostly bookkeeping no reader selects, so with the
0.25 s coalescing gap the full read ran about 4 times a second.

kanban_annotation_parts takes one key per part before the read and the
holder forces only the parts whose key moved since their last forced
read:
- counts: board and shadow content revisions, origin ledger, plain inputs
- links: board content revisions, origin ledger, plain inputs
- attention: board content revisions, files the done checks declared
Plain inputs (state.db, hub db, config, mutation cue) use
kanban_annotation_watch.signature. Every part is still forced when a
provider deadline came due, a board has no content revision and its stat
is not settled, a done check declared no watch paths, a key is unreadable,
the previous read failed, or the scope has no holder read yet. The counts
are also re-read once their last read is STRICT_REFRESH_AGE_S old, so the
published read_at stays adoptable. force_read.scope alone keeps meaning
"every part". Waiting sources are not gated: they run on every refresh
and own their input memo.

Sessions route. stamp_boards opened every board through the lock guard on
every request (58% of the route's samples, 10% more in the close). It now
keeps each board's contribution under the board file's change signature,
read once per request before any open; an unchanged board is not opened.
A board with a scheduled parked card (the only cards with an external
state, which also moves with the clock) keeps the 5 s bound
session_external already had.

Not changed: _project_remote_links (shared with the feed thread,
t_3d9583999ea5284c), the waiting sources and done checks themselves
(hermes-mods), payload shapes.

Tests: test_kanban_annotation_parts (a write to one source rereads only
the parts that read it; a bookkeeping write rereads none; every gated
refresh equals a cold full read; a due deadline, an undeclared check and
a failed read force everything; 40 writes through the real loop are a
bounded number of reads with the last write shown) and four new cases in
test_kanban_external_activity (an unchanged board is not opened over 20
requests, a write is seen on the next request, cached answer byte-equal
to an uncached one). Forcing every part again fails 5 of the 6 parts
tests; never storing the board contribution fails 3 of the 4 route tests.
120 adjacent test files: 1742 passed, 0 failed, 15 skipped.

Not measured live yet: the hub numbers are taken after deploy.
